WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.300
What is God’s patience inviting us to

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:05.620
do?

3
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.260
In Romans two,

4
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.080
Paul challenges the person who judges others

5
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.120
while practicing the same things.

6
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.560
Then he asks whether we are taking

7
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.260
God’s kindness for granted.

8
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.620
His kindness is meant to lead us

9
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:19.260
to repentance.

10
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.060
We can mistake a quiet season for

11
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:22.580
approval,

12
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.060
as though nothing going wrong means nothing

13
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:25.900
needs to change.

14
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.820
Paul teaches us to receive patience as

15
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.820
an opportunity to turn to God.

16
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.860
So when Scripture exposes a sin you

17
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:34.840
have been excusing,

18
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.000
name it honestly before him.

19
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.480
Ask for his mercy,

20
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.740
and take the next faithful step.

21
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.180
Let kindness lead you to repentance.
